# Extension build-time env vars (WXT/Vite inlines anything prefixed WXT_).
# All optional — defaults in code are fine for prod builds.
#
# Put dev-only overrides in .env.development.local — loaded by `pnpm dev`
# (mode=development) only; `pnpm build` (mode=production) never reads it.
# Don't use .env.local: Vite loads it in EVERY mode, so an override there
# would bake into the committed extension/ build (export-extension.sh
# refuses to run while one exists).

# Point everything cloud-bound at a local backend instead of https://api.airglow.dev.
# WXT_CLOUD_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3002

# Override PostHog project (e.g. point a dev build at a separate test project).
# Empty/absent → falls back to the public default key embedded in lib/posthog.ts.
# WXT_POSTHOG_KEY=phc_…
# WXT_POSTHOG_HOST=https://us.i.posthog.com

# Google sign-in OAuth client id (public value, not a secret). The default is
# baked into lib/airglow-auth.ts — this override exists only for forks pointing
# at their own Google Cloud project. A single "Web application"-type client
# drives the launchWebAuthFlow popup on every Chromium browser; its redirect
# https://<ext-id>.chromiumapp.org/ must be registered per extension id.
# WXT_GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID=….apps.googleusercontent.com
